# The build context is the source tree and nothing else. `target/` alone is
# tens of gigabytes and would be uploaded to the daemon on every build; the
# builder stage keeps its own compilation cache in a BuildKit cache mount.
/target
/.git
/.github

# Never in an image: weights, goldens, benchmark output, and the local design
# draft (AGENTS.md).
#
# These are NOT .gitignore semantics, which is the trap. Docker's `*` does not
# cross a `/`, so a bare `*.gguf` matches only the context root — it let the
# whole of /models through once the checkpoints moved in-tree. Anything meant
# to match at depth needs `**/`.
#
# /models/ is excluded as a directory for the same reason .gitignore does it:
# the HuggingFace download caches sitting beside the weights are not named
# `*.gguf` and would ship on their own. Compose bind-mounts it at /models at
# run time, so nothing in the build needs it.
/models/
**/*.gguf
**/*.safetensors
/goldens/
/.golden/
/bench-results/
/qwen36-rust-engine-plan.md

# Editor and agent scratch.
/.omc
/.claude
**/*.rs.bk
**/*.pdb

# Nothing under here affects the binary, and a change to one of them should
# not invalidate the build cache.
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# Compose reads .env at run time; it must never be baked into a layer.
/.env
